From 191d4c9ae6c62fab3694197d89b51f4fe98ce9d6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Micheal Waltz <micheal@ecliptik.com>
Date: Mon, 1 Jun 2026 08:42:58 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] dos: patch 0085 -- Bug-5 (#31) flip-tail bisection S1+S2
 DOS_Yield pin

Round-3 of the flip-tail bisection (markers-only; AppMinimized / stages[1005]
OOB / SDL_GetWindowSurface / DV-present all REFUTED). nx-engine localized the
organya title-hang to flip()'s COMMON tail (Renderer.cpp 5436->5751),
contained in flip_n=1 (flip never returned). The only scheduler-entering call
in that span is the per-flip SDL_Delay(0) at Renderer.cpp:5500 ->
SDL_SYS_DelayNS(0) -> DOS_Yield(). This is the SDL half: it pins whether main
parks inside DOS_Yield, names what it parks on, and confirms/refutes the
cooperative-starvation mechanism (the in-band organya stream never lets the
audio thread yield back to main).

S1 (timer/dos/SDL_systimer.c, ns==0 path): one-shot armed breadcrumbs
bracketing the DOS_Yield call -- "pre-DOS_Yield" / "post-DOS_Yield RETURNED".
Pairs with engine T2/T3 at 5500. engine-T2 + S1-pre with neither S1-post nor
engine-T3 => main PARKED inside DOS_Yield. Setting g_dos_starve_diag_in_delay0
around the call scopes the S2 scheduler breadcrumbs to THIS ns==0 call (the
present-path DelayPrecise uses ns!=0 and so does not trip them).

S2 (core/dos/SDL_dos_scheduler.c, DOS_Yield body): the contract floated a
"DOS_Yield spins on the SB16 device->lock" hypothesis, but DOS_Yield holds NO
lock and never spins -- pure round-robin (FindNextRunnable -> setjmp -> mark
prev READY -> longjmp). The device->lock regime (SDL/0068) lives in
SDL_DOSAudioPump, which is past T7 in run_tick, NOT on the flip-tail. The real
park-point is the longjmp. Breadcrumbs (one-shot, scoped to the flip-tail
ns==0 call on the main thread, prev/current_thread==0):
  - FindNextRunnable=next switch ("main->threadN longjmp, no return until
    re-sched") -- main handed the CPU to thread N and parks.
  - FindNextRunnable=-1 ("no other READY; returns to main -- self-deadlock
    candidate") -- its ABSENCE in the wedge confirms main parked at the switch.
  - "main RESUMED" in the resumed branch -- if switch logs but RESUMED + S1-post
    never do, main is parked at the longjmp = cooperative starvation.
FindNextRunnable's result is the sole (a)/(b) discriminator (cb_fills is
~120/sec, IRQ/DMA-driven, and says nothing about main's scheduling): N=audio
thread => audio-thread monopoly (case a); -1 => self-deadlock (case b, main is
the sole producer of the in-band stream).

S2 (audio/dos/SDL_dosaudio_sb.c) -- the smoking gun, no new LOG line:
  - g_dos_wd_room_returns (WaitDevice room-available return, sb.c room path) vs
    g_dos_wd_ringfull_yields (WaitDevice ring-full DOS_Yield) counters, APPENDED
    to patch 0082's existing every-100-cb_fills starve-diag/snd: line (zero
    added fsync). room climbs unbounded / yield_full FROZEN under organya ==
    the audio thread takes the no-yield path every wake and never yields back
    = mechanism CONFIRMED. (Under in-band organya the mix is non-silent, so the
    PlayDevice silence-skip SDL_Delay(10) throttle -- the out-of-band opl3/WB
    yield path -- never fires; the only other yield is ring-full, which never
    happens while the stream starves.)
  - one-shot "audio-thread raw_tid=N" (DOS_GetCurrentThreadID()-1, normalized
    to scheduler's raw index) identifies the thread that pulls the organya
    stream. Matching FindNextRunnable=next against it answers self-deadlock
    (b) vs monopoly (a) from the SDL side (nx engine cannot see the DOS thread
    context).

Object note: organya is a standalone SDL3 audio STREAM (organyaStreamCallback
via SDL_SetAudioStreamGetCallback), NOT an SDL3_mixer source -- the markers
target the device-output / stream path.

Scoping: g_dos_starve_diag_in_delay0 (defined in the scheduler TU) is set true
ONLY by SDL_SYS_DelayNS's ns==0 path; the switch breadcrumb is additionally
gated on prev==0 so the audio thread's own DOS_Yield calls (which see the flag
leaked-true while main is parked) do not mis-fire. S1/S2 latch on the FIRST
armed SDL_Delay(0) -- cross-check S1-pre's t vs engine T2's t to confirm it is
the 5500 tail call (the heavy present yielder is ns!=0, so it cannot consume
them).

Gate: STARVE_DIAG=1 + g_title_diag_armed (mirrors SDL/0082/0083; no new env
var, no BOOT.md edit). One-shot per breadcrumb; the room/yield counters ride
0082's existing emit (two unconditional adds, read only under STARVE_DIAG).
Default OFF. S3 link-check: g_dos_starve_diag_in_delay0 + DOS_GetCurrentThreadID
resolve in libSDL3.a; the wd counters are sb.c-local statics; g_title_diag_armed
resolves from the engine at final link (same as 0084). The fix class this
points to (make the in-band stream-refill path yield like the silence throttle)
is FLAGGED ONLY -- not authored this round; markers confirm the mechanism on
g2k first. Workspace-local; never upstreamed.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 src/audio/dos/SDL_dosaudio_sb.c  | 34 +++++++++++++++
 src/core/dos/SDL_dos_scheduler.c | 71 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 src/timer/dos/SDL_systimer.c     | 52 +++++++++++++++++++++++
 3 files changed, 157 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/audio/dos/SDL_dosaudio_sb.c b/src/audio/dos/SDL_dosaudio_sb.c
index 58fd29ec2..60437aa29 100644
--- a/src/audio/dos/SDL_dosaudio_sb.c
+++ b/src/audio/dos/SDL_dosaudio_sb.c
@@ -1408,6 +1408,21 @@ static void MaybeServiceIdlePauseRequests(void)
     }
 }
 
+/* DOSKUTSU patch (SDL/0085): Bug-5 (#31) WaitDevice yield-asymmetry counters.
+   The decisive S2 read for the organya title-hang. WaitDevice's two outcomes:
+   ring has room -> return WITHOUT yielding (room-available path); ring full ->
+   DOS_Yield. Under in-band organya the mix is non-silent (so the silence-skip
+   SDL_Delay(10) throttle in PlayDevice never fires) and the stream starves
+   (avail=0), so the audio thread takes the room-available path on every wake
+   and NEVER reaches the ring-full DOS_Yield -- it never cooperatively yields
+   back to main. These counters make that empirical: g_dos_wd_room_returns
+   climbs unbounded while g_dos_wd_ringfull_yields stays FROZEN == mechanism
+   CONFIRMED. They are APPENDED to patch 0082's existing every-100-cb_fills
+   starve-diag/snd: line (no new LOG line, zero added fsync). Always incremented
+   (two adds; read only under STARVE_DIAG). Workspace-local; never upstreamed. */
+static Uint32 g_dos_wd_room_returns    = 0;  /* WaitDevice room-available returns (no yield) */
+static Uint32 g_dos_wd_ringfull_yields = 0;  /* WaitDevice ring-full DOS_Yield count */
+
 // Wait until the ring buffer has room for one more chunk.
 // The audio thread keeps yielding so the game's main thread can run while
 // we wait. Because the ISR is steadily draining the ring, this only blocks
@@ -1499,6 +1514,7 @@ static bool DOSSOUNDBLASTER_WaitDevice(SDL_AudioDevice *device)
             if (g_p12_sdl_audio_instr_active) {
                 g_p12_sdl_audio_thread_ns += SDL_GetTicksNS() - _p12_wait_t0;
             }
+            g_dos_wd_room_returns++; /* SDL/0085 S2: room-available, NO yield */
             return true; // room for at least one chunk
         }
 
@@ -1565,6 +1581,7 @@ static bool DOSSOUNDBLASTER_WaitDevice(SDL_AudioDevice *device)
             }
         }
 
+        g_dos_wd_ringfull_yields++; /* SDL/0085 S2: ring full -> cooperative yield */
         DOS_Yield();
     }
 }
@@ -3022,6 +3039,18 @@ static bool DOSSOUNDBLASTER_PlayDevice(SDL_AudioDevice *device, const Uint8 *buf
             if (s_sd_enabled) {
                 dos_port_dbg_log("audio: SDL/0082 STARVE_DIAG=1 -- Bug-5 ring/"
                                  "silent-IRQ starve markers ENABLED (snd: layer)");
+                /* DOSKUTSU patch (SDL/0085): record the SDL playback audio
+                   thread's RAW scheduler index (DOS_GetCurrentThreadID()-1, to
+                   match scheduler.c's FindNextRunnable/`next` index; the API
+                   returns index+1). PlayDevice runs on this thread, so this is
+                   the thread that pulls the organya stream. The bisection
+                   matches scheduler S2 FindNextRunnable=next against this id:
+                   next==audio_raw_tid => main switched to the audio thread =
+                   monopoly (case a); FindNextRunnable=-1 => self-deadlock
+                   (case b, main is the sole stream producer). One-shot. */
+                dos_port_dbg_log("starve-diag/snd: S2 audio-thread raw_tid=%d "
+                                 "(pulls the organya stream)",
+                                 DOS_GetCurrentThreadID() - 1);
             }
         }
         s_sd_calls++;
@@ -3036,12 +3065,17 @@ static bool DOSSOUNDBLASTER_PlayDevice(SDL_AudioDevice *device, const Uint8 *buf
                 dos_port_dbg_log(
                     "audio: starve-diag/snd: t=%lu avail=%d chunk=%d "
                     "consec_silent=%lu silent_total=%lu cb_fills=%lu "
+                    "room_returns=%lu yield_full=%lu "
                     "paused=%d pause_req=%d%s",
                     (unsigned long)SDL_GetTicks(),
                     sd_avail, isr_chunk_size,
                     (unsigned long)isr_consecutive_silent_irqs,
                     (unsigned long)dos_port_audio_silent_irq_count,
                     (unsigned long)s_sd_calls,
+                    /* SDL/0085 S2 yield-asymmetry: room climbs / yield_full
+                       FROZEN under organya == audio thread never yields back. */
+                    (unsigned long)g_dos_wd_room_returns,
+                    (unsigned long)g_dos_wd_ringfull_yields,
                     (int)isr_dsp_paused, (int)g_dos_audio_pause_request,
                     sd_low ? " LOW" : "");
             }
diff --git a/src/core/dos/SDL_dos_scheduler.c b/src/core/dos/SDL_dos_scheduler.c
index 9c0163ce1..4337a4b34 100644
--- a/src/core/dos/SDL_dos_scheduler.c
+++ b/src/core/dos/SDL_dos_scheduler.c
@@ -25,6 +25,7 @@
 
 #include "SDL_dos.h"
 #include "SDL_dos_scheduler.h"
+#include "../../video/dos/SDL_dosdbg.h" /* DOSKUTSU patch 0085: dos_port_dbg_log (no-op macro off-DOSVESA) */
 #include <setjmp.h>
 
 /* DJGPP's jmp_buf is defined as:
@@ -42,6 +43,31 @@ static DOS_ThreadContext threads[DOS_MAX_THREADS];
 static int current_thread = 0; // Index of currently running thread
 static bool scheduler_initialized = false;
 
+/* DOSKUTSU patch (SDL/0085): Bug-5 (#31) flip-tail bisection S2 -- name where
+   main parks inside DOS_Yield. The flip-tail SDL_Delay(0) (Renderer.cpp:5500)
+   is the only scheduler-entering call in flip()'s common tail; this pins
+   whether main reaches the longjmp (switches to the audio thread) and never
+   gets re-scheduled (cooperative starvation -- the audio thread's only yield
+   under in-band organya is WaitDevice ring-full, which never fires when the
+   ring starves; the silence-skip SDL_Delay(10) throttle fires only for
+   out-of-band backends like opl3) vs. DOS_Yield returning normally.
+
+   CORRECTION to the contract's S2 framing: DOS_Yield's body holds NO lock and
+   never spins. The SB16 device->lock cooperative-starvation regime (SDL/0068)
+   lives in SDL_DOSAudioPump, a path NOT on the flip-tail (the tail's only
+   yielder is SDL_Delay(0)). The park-point is the longjmp itself: main's
+   setjmp does not return until another thread longjmps back to it. So the
+   breadcrumb sits at the longjmp + the resumed branch.
+
+   g_dos_starve_diag_in_delay0 is set true by SDL_SYS_DelayNS's ns==0 path only
+   (the present-path DelayPrecise uses ns!=0, so it does NOT trip S2), and the
+   switch breadcrumb is additionally gated on prev==0 (main thread) so the audio
+   thread's own DOS_Yield calls -- which see the flag leaked-true while main is
+   parked -- do not mis-fire. One-shot per site. Markers-only; read-only w.r.t.
+   scheduling. Default OFF (flag false). Workspace-local; never upstreamed. */
+extern volatile bool g_title_diag_armed;            /* nxengine 0194, extern "C" */
+volatile bool g_dos_starve_diag_in_delay0 = false;  /* set by SDL_SYS_DelayNS(0) */
+
 // Find the next runnable thread using round-robin scheduling.
 // Returns thread ID, or -1 if no other thread is runnable.
 static int FindNextRunnable(int start)
@@ -192,6 +218,22 @@ void DOS_Yield(void)
 
     int next = FindNextRunnable(current_thread);
     if (next < 0) {
+        /* DOSKUTSU patch (SDL/0085): S2 FindNextRunnable=-1 breadcrumb. No other
+           thread is READY, so DOS_Yield returns to main immediately (no switch).
+           In the organya wedge this should NOT fire (the audio thread is READY,
+           so the switch branch below logs instead); its PRESENCE would mean main
+           is the sole runnable context => self-deadlock (case b: main is the sole
+           producer of the in-band organya stream, yielding forever waiting for
+           itself). Scoped to the flip-tail SDL_Delay(0) on main. One-shot. */
+        if (g_dos_starve_diag_in_delay0 && current_thread == 0) {
+            static bool _bcd_s2nrun = false;
+            if (!_bcd_s2nrun) {
+                dos_port_dbg_log("starve-diag/snd: S2 DOS_Yield FindNextRunnable=-1 "
+                                 "(no other READY; returns to main -- self-deadlock "
+                                 "candidate) t=%lu", (unsigned long)SDL_GetTicks());
+                _bcd_s2nrun = true;
+            }
+        }
         return; // No other runnable thread, continue current
     }
 
@@ -204,6 +246,21 @@ void DOS_Yield(void)
             threads[prev].state = DOS_THREAD_READY;
         }
 
+        /* DOSKUTSU patch (SDL/0085): S2 switch breadcrumb. main is about to
+           longjmp to thread `next` and will not return to this frame until it
+           is re-scheduled. Scoped to the flip-tail SDL_Delay(0)
+           (g_dos_starve_diag_in_delay0) on the main thread (prev==0). One-shot. */
+        if (g_dos_starve_diag_in_delay0 && prev == 0) {
+            static bool _bcd_s2switch = false;
+            if (!_bcd_s2switch) {
+                dos_port_dbg_log("starve-diag/snd: S2 DOS_Yield FindNextRunnable=%d "
+                                 "(main->thread%d longjmp, no return until re-sched; "
+                                 "match vs audio-thread raw_tid => monopoly case a) t=%lu",
+                                 next, next, (unsigned long)SDL_GetTicks());
+                _bcd_s2switch = true;
+            }
+        }
+
         // Switch to next thread
         current_thread = next;
         threads[next].state = DOS_THREAD_RUNNING;
@@ -214,6 +271,20 @@ void DOS_Yield(void)
         longjmp(threads[next].env, 1);
     }
     // else: we've been switched back to — just return
+
+    /* DOSKUTSU patch (SDL/0085): S2 resume breadcrumb. main was re-scheduled
+       (another thread longjmp'd back into this frame; current_thread is now 0).
+       If S2-switch logged but this never does -- alongside S1 post-DOS_Yield
+       missing -- main is parked at the longjmp = cooperative starvation (the
+       audio thread never yielded back). One-shot. */
+    if (g_dos_starve_diag_in_delay0 && current_thread == 0) {
+        static bool _bcd_s2resume = false;
+        if (!_bcd_s2resume) {
+            dos_port_dbg_log("starve-diag/snd: S2 DOS_Yield main RESUMED "
+                             "(re-scheduled) t=%lu", (unsigned long)SDL_GetTicks());
+            _bcd_s2resume = true;
+        }
+    }
 }
 
 void DOS_ExitThread(int status)
diff --git a/src/timer/dos/SDL_systimer.c b/src/timer/dos/SDL_systimer.c
index d47bae177..208a31b80 100644
--- a/src/timer/dos/SDL_systimer.c
+++ b/src/timer/dos/SDL_systimer.c
@@ -26,6 +26,36 @@
 #include <time.h> /* uclock, uclock_t, UCLOCKS_PER_SEC */
 
 #include "../../core/dos/SDL_dos_scheduler.h"
+#include "../../video/dos/SDL_dosdbg.h" /* DOSKUTSU patch 0085: dos_port_dbg_log (no-op macro off-DOSVESA) */
+
+/* DOSKUTSU patch (SDL/0085): Bug-5 (#31) flip-tail bisection S1 -- bracket the
+   flip-tail SDL_Delay(0) -> SDL_SYS_DelayNS(0) -> DOS_Yield call (the only
+   scheduler-entering call in flip()'s common tail, Renderer.cpp:5500). Pairs
+   with engine T2/T3: if engine T2 (pre-SDL_Delay) + this "pre-DOS_Yield" log
+   and neither "post-DOS_Yield RETURNED" nor engine T3 fire -> main PARKED
+   inside DOS_Yield. Setting g_dos_starve_diag_in_delay0 (defined in the
+   scheduler TU) around the call arms the S2 breadcrumbs inside DOS_Yield to
+   fire ONLY for this ns==0 path -- the present-path DelayPrecise yielder uses
+   ns!=0 and so does not trip them. Gate = STARVE_DIAG=1 + g_title_diag_armed
+   (mirrors SDL/0082/0083). One-shot per site; default OFF.
+
+   CAVEAT (read in the log): S1/S2 latch on the FIRST armed SDL_Delay(0). The
+   heavy present-path yielder is ns!=0 so it cannot consume them, but cross-
+   check S1-pre's t against engine T2's t to confirm this IS the 5500 tail call
+   (low risk -- arming is at title_init, the tail is the first SDL_Delay(0)).
+   Workspace-local; never upstreamed. */
+extern volatile bool g_title_diag_armed;          /* nxengine 0194, extern "C" */
+extern volatile bool g_dos_starve_diag_in_delay0; /* scheduler TU (SDL/0085) */
+static int s_sd085_enabled = -1;                  /* -1 unread; cached strict-1 STARVE_DIAG */
+
+static bool _sd085_active(void)
+{
+    if (s_sd085_enabled < 0) {
+        const char *sd = SDL_GetHint("SDL_HINT_DOS_STARVE_DIAG");
+        s_sd085_enabled = (sd && sd[0] == '1' && sd[1] == '\0') ? 1 : 0;
+    }
+    return s_sd085_enabled == 1 && g_title_diag_armed;
+}
 
 /* DJGPP's uclock() reprograms PIT channel 0 for a higher tick rate on first
    call, giving ~1.19 MHz resolution (UCLOCKS_PER_SEC == 1193180).  This is
@@ -45,6 +75,28 @@ Uint64 SDL_GetPerformanceFrequency(void)
 void SDL_SYS_DelayNS(Uint64 ns)
 {
     if (ns == 0) {
+        /* DOSKUTSU patch (SDL/0085): S1 flip-tail SDL_Delay(0) bracket + S2 arm.
+           One-shot, armed window only; g_dos_starve_diag_in_delay0 scopes the
+           DOS_Yield-body breadcrumbs to this call. The clear after DOS_Yield is
+           NOT reached if main parks inside (wedge) -- harmless, the flag staying
+           true only keeps S2 armed and prev==0 excludes the audio thread. */
+        if (_sd085_active()) {
+            static bool _bcd_s1pre = false, _bcd_s1post = false;
+            if (!_bcd_s1pre) {
+                dos_port_dbg_log("starve-diag/snd: S1 SDL_SYS_DelayNS(0) "
+                                 "pre-DOS_Yield t=%lu", (unsigned long)SDL_GetTicks());
+                _bcd_s1pre = true;
+            }
+            g_dos_starve_diag_in_delay0 = true;
+            DOS_Yield();
+            g_dos_starve_diag_in_delay0 = false;
+            if (!_bcd_s1post) {
+                dos_port_dbg_log("starve-diag/snd: S1 SDL_SYS_DelayNS(0) "
+                                 "post-DOS_Yield RETURNED t=%lu", (unsigned long)SDL_GetTicks());
+                _bcd_s1post = true;
+            }
+            return;
+        }
         DOS_Yield();
         return;
     }
